Robin, I am admirative of the way you try to inculcate your baby lojbanic
notions.

Nevertheless, I wonder it may be senseless to teach lojban in such a way,
because it is basically the way we learn natlangs.   I sincerely doubt
anybody can guess the way Lojban works on the sole basis of trials&errors,
rather it seems to me that such an artifical logical language can only be
taught in a prescriptive kind of professoral way.   At least, by reading
manuals, and having a priori strong notions of grammar and formal logic...

Regards, Escape


2013/7/8 Robin Lee Powell <rlpowell@digitalkingdom.org>

